First, we need to define the decision variables, objective function, and constraints of the problem. The decision variables represent the amount of each product to produce, and the objective function represents the total profit. The constraints represent the demand, capacity, and resource limitations.
Here's an example Scala code to formulate the problem as an MILP model:
```
import com.google.ortools.linearsolver.MPSolver
import com.google.ortools.linearsolver.MPVariable
import com.google.ortools.linearsolver.MPObjective
import com.google.ortools.linearsolver.MPConstraint
val solver = new MPSolver("Production Planning", MPSolver.OptimizationProblemType.CBC_MIXED_INTEGER_PROGRAMMING)
// Define decision variables
val numProducts = 3
val x = Array.tabulate(numProducts)(i => solver.makeIntVar(0.0, Double.POSITIVE_INFINITY, s"x$i"))
// Define objective function
val costs = Array(10.0, 15.0, 20.0)
val profits = Array(20.0, 25.0, 30.0)
val objective = solver.objective()
for (i <- 0 until numProducts) {
  objective.setCoefficient(x(i), profits(i) - costs(i))
}
objective.setMaximization()
// Define demand constraints
val demands = Array(100.0, 150.0, 200.0)
for (i <- 0 until numProducts) {
  val demandConstraint = solver.makeConstraint(0.0, demands(i), s"demand$i")
  demandConstraint.setCoefficient(x(i), 1.0)
}
// Define capacity constraints
val capacities = Array(500.0, 750.0, 1000.0)
for (j <- 0 until numResources) {
  val capacityConstraint = solver.makeConstraint(0.0, capacities(j), s"capacity$j")
  for (i <- 0 until numProducts) {
    capacityConstraint.setCoefficient(x(i), resourceUsage(i)(j))
  }
}
// Define resource constraints
val labor = solver.makeConstraint(0.0, 500.0, "labor")
val materials = solver.makeConstraint(0.0, 1000.0, "materials")
for (i <- 0 until numProducts) {
  labor.setCoefficient(x(i), laborUsage(i))
  materials.setCoefficient(x(i), materialUsage(i))
}
// Solve the problem
val resultStatus = solver.solve()
// Interpret the results
if (resultStatus == MPSolver.ResultStatus.OPTIMAL) {
  println("Optimal solution found.")
  println("Total profit: " + objective.value())
