function isValidHTMLCode(code) {
  const regex = /<([a-z]+)([^<]+)*(?:>(.*)<\/\1>|\s+\/>)/gi;
  return regex.test(code);
}
```
The function takes a string `code` as input and returns a boolean value indicating whether it is a valid HTML code or not. The regular expression used in the function matches opening and closing tags of HTML elements, and checks if they are properly nested and closed. 
