One way to integrate AI technology into Java code to sort a list of numbers is by using a machine learning algorithm. One such algorithm is the neural network, which can learn to recognize patterns in data and make predictions based on those patterns.
Here is an example code snippet that uses a neural network to sort a list of numbers in ascending order:
```
import java.util.Arrays;
import org.neuroph.core.NeuralNetwork;
import org.neuroph.core.data.DataSet;
import org.neuroph.core.data.DataSetRow;
import org.neuroph.nnet.MultiLayerPerceptron;
public class NeuralSort {
  public static void main(String[] args) {
    // Create a list of numbers to be sorted
    double[] numbers = {5.4, 2.1, 8.7, 1.3, 9.0};
    // Create a neural network with one input and one output neuron
    NeuralNetwork neuralNet = new MultiLayerPerceptron(1, 5, 1);
    // Create a training dataset with the list of numbers as input and output
    DataSet trainingSet = new DataSet(1, 1);
    for (double number : numbers) {
      trainingSet.addRow(new DataSetRow(new double[] {number}, new double[] {number}));
    }
    // Train the neural network on the training dataset
    neuralNet.learn(trainingSet);
    // Use the neural network to sort the list of numbers
    double[] sortedNumbers = new double[numbers.length];
    for (int i = 0; i < numbers.length; i++) {
      sortedNumbers[i] = neuralNet.calculate(new double[] {numbers[i]})[0];
    }
    // Print the sorted list of numbers
    System.out.println(Arrays.toString(sortedNumbers));
  }
}
```
In this example, we create a list of numbers and a neural network with one input neuron (representing the number to be sorted) and one output neuron (representing the sorted number). We then create a training dataset with the list of numbers as input and output, and train the neural network on the dataset.
Finally, we use the neural network to sort the list of numbers by feeding each number into the neural network and collecting the output. The resulting sorted list of numbers is printed to the console.

